+### V-46 (Medium) Phone: nothing on the chart says the axis is US dollars a year
+- View: Chart, Clusters and Ranges, 390 px. Repro: `#c=amazon` on a phone.
+- Expected: the axis names its unit, as on desktop ("Yearly pay, US$ (converted)").
+- Actual: the axis reads "$0 $100K $200K $300K" with no caption, and neither "a year" nor "US$" is visible
+  anywhere in the chart; "Pay is yearly, in approx US dollars" is behind Details. On Amazon that axis holds 2,908
+  postings worked out from hourly pay and 803 converted from other currencies. `renderAxis()` has a narrow
+  caption ("US$ a year, converted"), but it is only drawn when the label column is wider than 0, and on a phone
+  that column is always 0, so the narrow caption is dead code. The median caption ("Median base pay $141K") is
+  missing on phones for the same reason.
+- Screenshots: `clusters-amazon-390-light.png`, `ranges-amazon-390-light.png`. Owner: `chart.js renderAxis()`,
+  `renderHist()` (`labelW > 0`).
+
+### V-48 (Medium) On-target earnings: the dashed bars have no legend key, and OTE level spans are drawn striped
+- View: Chart, Ranges. Repro: `#c=nvidia&v=ranges`; main site `#c=anthropic&v=ranges`.
+- Expected (V-20, fix wave 4): on-target earnings dashed, "with legend keys".
+- Actual: the 41 NVIDIA and 47 Anthropic on-target bars are dashed (`ms-row__bar--ote`), but the legend has only
+  the department colours and "Striped: several levels or places"; nothing says what a dashed bar is. 11 NVIDIA
+  on-target ranges over two levels ("6 roles with the same posted range, $224K to $397K, on-target earnings, spans
+  2 levels, Account Manager") are drawn striped, because a span wins over OTE in `buildRow()`, so they look like
+  base-pay spans.
+- Screenshots: `v-nvidia-ranges-ote.png`, `v-anthropic-ranges-ote.png`. Owner: `chart.js renderLegend()`,
+  `buildRow()`.
+
+### V-47 (Medium) Amazon: a filter, a sort, Group by and a zoom take 0.3–1.3 s on desktop
+- Measured on the reviewer build, 1440 px, 3 runs each, from the click to the last change, at load 12–16 on 4 CPUs
+  (other agents' test runs): department filter 358–560 ms; sort 291–651 ms; Group by seniority 546–783 ms (long
+  tasks 465–721 ms), by location 458–700 ms; Clusters → Ranges 407–1,306 ms; Ranges by department 315–699 ms; map
+  zoom 446–906 ms (Leaflet's 250 ms animation included; long tasks 117–435 ms). The chart's own `update()` on the
+  22,179 postings, timed alone in the page, takes 75–205 ms (median 80–149 ms per view); the rest is the app's
+  filtering, list and Juice. Everything is over the brief's 200 ms, but the load was 3–4× the CPU count, so the
+  numbers are high by an unknown factor.
+- No test, as with V-31: it passes or fails with the machine's load. Owner: `public/app.js` (filter, list render,
+  `scheduleViz()`), `chart.js renderClusters()` (up to four planning passes).
+
